Which one to pick:

  * Choose Apache-2.0 if you want the express patent grant and the patent
    retaliation clause, or if your organisation's policy requires an SPDX
    licence with a patent grant.  Redistribution must keep this file, the
    NOTICE file and the licence text, and must mark modified files.
  * Choose BSD-3-Clause if you want the shortest set of obligations: keep the
    copyright notice, keep the disclaimer, and do not use the authors' names
    to endorse your fork.  There is no NOTICE requirement and no
    "state your changes" requirement.

Neither licence is conditioned on how you use the software, and neither one
grants permission to attack a network you do not own or have written
authorisation to test.  Authorisation is a matter of law and of the contract
with the site, not of the software licence — see docs/ETHICS-AND-LEGAL.md.

Unless you explicitly state otherwise, any contribution you intentionally
submit for inclusion in this project is dual-licensed under these same two
licences, with no additional terms or conditions.
